label confrontation
[signal arg="bg:east_wall_path"]
Leonora (Default): Walk with me.
She led him away from the main courtyard along the quiet east wall, and didn't speak again until they were well clear of anyone who might overhear.
Leonora (Confused): I've had two days to decide how angry I am about this, and I still haven't managed it, which is not an experience I enjoy.
Lan (Default): I could apologize, if it would help.
Leonora (Default): It wouldn't. You don't know what you'd be apologizing for yet.
Leonora (Mad): Three weeks ago I broke your guard in under ten seconds and told you not to waste my morning.
Leonora (Mad): Two days ago I watched you cut through six trained killers like it was the easiest thing you'd done all year.
Leonora (Mad): Those two facts do not belong to the same person, Schwert. I want to know which one was the lie.
Lan (Default): Neither. The guard I gave you in Amir's class was deliberately bad. What you saw in the forest was real.
Leonora (Default): So you can fight. Properly. And you chose to let the academy believe you couldn't. Why.
Lan (Default): Because the moment people know what I can actually do, I stop being a student and start being useful to somebody.
Lan (Default): A noble house. A faction. A war I didn't start. I'd rather be underestimated than owned.
Leonora (Confused): That's either the most cynical thing I've heard from a commoner since I arrived, or the most honest. I haven't decided which.
Lan (Smug): They're not always different things.
Leonora (Default): No. They're really not.
label thanks
Leonora (Default): You saved my life.
Leonora (Default): I've thought about how to say that since it happened, and every version sounded either too small or too dramatic, so I'm going to say it badly.
Leonora (Default): You saved my life, and I have no idea why a rank {rank} commoner with something to hide would risk exposing his one advantage to do it.
Lan (Default): You needed saving. I was there. It didn't feel complicated at the time.
Leonora (Default): I've spent my entire life being protected by people who wanted something from it afterward.
Leonora (Default): A title, a favor, my father's attention. You gained nothing.
Leonora (Default): So either you're a fool, which I don't believe, or your reasons are something I haven't worked out yet.
Lan (Sus): (What I want to say is I've known this ambush was coming since before I met you, because I lived this story before, on a screen, in another world.)
Lan (Default): Some things I can't explain. Not won't. Can't. If I tried, you'd like me even less than you do right now.
Leonora (Smile): That is the first thing you've said tonight I actually believe completely.
Leonora (Smile): Everyone who lies to me tries to make the lie sound complete.
Leonora (Smile): You told me there's a piece missing and didn't fill the gap with something convincing.
label condition
Leonora (Default): Here's what I've decided. I'm not going to report what I saw.
Leonora (Default): Not to my own people, not to the faculty beyond whatever Berthram already knows.
Leonora (Default): Your secret is safe from me, for now, on one condition.
Lan (Smug): I'm starting to think everyone in this school keeps a list of conditions.
Leonora (Smile): Then you're finally understanding how this world works.
Leonora (Smile): Whatever's actually happening around my family that put six armed men in a forest with my name on their orders, you tell me the moment you can.
Leonora (Smile): The part that keeps me, or the people around me, alive.
Lan (Sus): You think there's more coming.
Leonora (Default): A princess doesn't get ambushed by six professionals over nothing, and whoever arranged it won't be satisfied with one failed attempt.
Leonora (Default): When I find out who did this, I'd like to already know whether you saw it coming.
Lan (Sus): (I did. And I can't say it.)
- "You'll hear it from me first."
	set {aff_leonora} += 1
	Lan (Default): If I ever know something that keeps you alive, you'll hear it from me before you hear it from anyone else.
- "I'll try to be less mysterious."
	Lan (Smug): I'll try to be less mysterious. No, really. I'll try.
	Lan (Default): If I ever know something that keeps you alive, you'll hear it from me first.
Lan (Default): That's the most honest promise I can make you right now.
Leonora (Default): I'll take it. For now.
Leonora (Default): For what it's worth, I owe you an apology. I called you a waste of a morning.
Leonora (Default): I should have known better than to judge a fighter by the guard he chose to lose with.
Lan (Smug): You weren't wrong to be annoyed. I was trying to make you annoyed.
Leonora (Smile): I know. It worked exceptionally well. I'd appreciate it if you didn't try that trick on me twice.
Lan (Smug): No promises.
She smiled, just slightly, and walked away toward the lit windows.
[signal arg="chapter_end:ch06"]
[end_timeline]
